    <p style="font-size: 10pt;">A PIN is any combination of five digits you choose except five zeros. If you use a PIN, there is nothing to sign and nothing to mail—not even your Form 1040-X.</p>
    <p style="font-size: 10pt;">Your electronic return is considered a validly signed return when you use a PIN. The date of birth, PIN, if applicable, and age from your originally filed prior year federal income tax return, if applicable. If you're filing jointly, you must use a PIN that both spouses agree to use. If you're filing single, you must use a PIN that you agree to use.</p>
